Install MariaDB's dev plugin on the first start

The extension installs MariaDB's dev plugin (github.com/mariadb/ai-plugins,
folder dev) once, in the background, with the bundled CLI
(`extensions install https://github.com/mariadb/ai-plugins:dev --consent`).
A plugin already in <QWEN_HOME or ~/.qwen>/extensions/dev counts as
installed. Success is recorded in globalState (mariadbDevPluginInstalled), so
an uninstalled plugin stays uninstalled; a failed install (offline) is only
logged and retried on the next activation. The daemon and the ACP process
wait for that install before they start, so their first start loads the
plugin. The setting qwen-code.installMariaDbPlugin (on by default) turns it
off.

